%S A400699 3,7,13,19,31,43,55,73,91,109,133,157,181,211,241,271,307,343,379,421,
%T A400699 463,505,553,601,649,703,757,811,871,931,991,1057,1123,1189,1261,1333,
%U A400699 1405,1483,1561,1639,1723,1807,1891,1981,2071,2161,2257,2353,2449,2551
%N A400699 Start with a set of three adjacent collinear points in a hexagonal lattice. Every iteration, add to the set the points in the lattice which are adjacent to at least two points already in the set. This sequence gives the number of points in the set after n iterations.
%H A400699 Aidan Markey, <a href="/A400699/a400699.pdf">Illustration of initial terms</a>
%H A400699 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1,1,-2,1).
%F A400699 a(n) = n^2 + 3*n + 1 if n == 0 (mod 3), and a(n) = n^2 + 3*n + 3 otherwise.
%F A400699 From _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 09 2026: (Start)
%F A400699 a(n) = 2*a(n-1) - a(n-2) + a(n-3) - 2*a(n-4) + a(n-5).
%F A400699 G.f.: (3+x+2*x^2-3*x^3+5*x^4-2*x^5) / ((1-x^3) * (1-x)^2)). (End)
%e A400699 See Links.
%Y A400699 Cf. A374338, A400700, A400701 (corresponding sequences for two, four, and five points).
%Y A400699 Cf. A008458, A338097.
%K A400699 nonn,new
%O A400699 0,1
%A A400699 _Aidan Markey_, Oct 03 2026
%E A400699 More terms from _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 09 2026
